4. Health Check Analysis: Probes and Outcomes
Probes are periodic diagnostics that determine the health of a container.
Liveness: Triggers container restart on failure. Default: Success.
Readiness: Removes Pod from Service endpoints on failure. Default state before initial delay: Failure.
Startup: Protects slow-starting apps; disables other probes until it succeeds. Default: Success.
Check Mechanisms
Mechanism
Success Criteria
exec
Command exit code 0.
grpc
Response status is SERVING.
httpGet
Status code ≥ 200 and < 400.
tcpSocket
Specified TCP port is open.
Architectural Note: The exec mechanism incurs significant CPU overhead due to process forking. In high-density clusters, utilize httpGet or tcpSocket where possible to maintain node performance.
