5. Monitoring Pod Conditions and Readiness
The PodStatus includes an array of PodConditions that provide granular visibility into the Pod's lifecycle progress.
Key Pod Conditions
PodScheduled: Pod has been assigned to a node.
Initialized: All init containers have successfully completed.
Ready: The Pod is healthy and capable of serving traffic.
ContainersReady: Every container in the Pod is in a ready state.
PodReadyToStartContainers (Beta): The sandbox and networking have been successfully configured by the CRI.
DisruptionTarget: Indicates the Pod is slated for termination due to eviction, preemption, or garbage collection.
Readiness Gates and Network Readiness
Readiness Gates allow external controllers to inject custom status signals. A Pod is only "Ready" when all containers are ready and all gates are True. The Pod Network Readiness flow ensures the kubelet does not pull images or start containers until the network sandbox is fully initialized (indicated by PodReadyToStartContainers).
