8. Scheduling Delays and Kubelet Behavior
Scheduling Readiness
Pods may be held in the Pending phase by scheduling gates. These gates must be removed by an external controller before the scheduler will consider the Pod for placement.
Kubelet Restarts and Feature Status
If a kubelet restarts, containers continue running.
Deprecated Feature (v1.35): The ChangeContainerStatusOnKubeletRestart feature gate is now deprecated and disabled by default. Relying on the legacy behavior (where containers were marked as not ready during a restart) is discouraged as it causes issues in large-scale environments.
Node Heartbeats: If a node fails heartbeats long enough, the control plane taints the node, eventually triggering Pod eviction.
Garbage Collection (PodGC)
The Pod Garbage Collector removes terminated Pods that exceed the terminated-pod-gc-threshold. It also targets orphan Pods (where the node is missing), unscheduled terminating Pods, and Pods on nodes tainted as out-of-service.
